 "description": "In the week of October 12-16, 2026, tech stocks had their worst week since June: the Nasdaq fell about 4.5%, chip stocks lost 11.4%, South Korea's Kospi dropped 7.7% in one day and memory chipmakers lost up to 24%. Why? Hotter-than-expected inflation (3.7%), higher interest rates and growing worries about the debt behind the AI building boom. Who it hits, what the worried and the calm camps say, and what to watch next. Explained with stick figures, facts only. Not financial advice.\n\nDave and Linda are made-up characters. Real people are shown as generic labelled stick figures; quotes are attributed as reported.\n\nSources:\nAP via Hartford Courant, US markets weighed down by extended sell-off in the tech sector (Oct 16, 2026): https://www.courant.com/2026/10/16/stock-market\nAP via Yahoo Finance, Deepening tech sell-off drags stocks lower as major markets slide (Oct 15, 2026): https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/deepening-tech-sell-off-drags-041902749.html\nYahoo Finance live blog, Oct 15, 2026 (CoreWeave, Apple, yields, quotes): https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/live/stock-market-today-dow-sp-500-rise-nasdaq-trims-losses-as-treasury-yields-sink-153611834.html\nInvesting.com / Reuters, Nasdaq notches worst week since late June with a 4.5% slide: https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/nasdaq-futures-edge-lower-as-ai-spending-fed-rate-concerns-weigh-4952930\nThe Telegraph, Global AI stocks sell-off spreads to Wall Street (Oct 15, 2026): https://www.telegraph.co.uk/business/2026/10/15/asian-markets-plunge-amid-tech-sell-off\nCNBC, AI stocks tumble in global tech rout on AI funding worries (Oct 15, 2026): https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/15/sk-hynix-samsung-softbank-stocks-asia-tech-rout-ai-funding-worries.html\nWSJ, Warsh Avoids Signal on October Rate Move: https://www.wsj.com/economy/central-banking/warsh-avoids-signal-on-october-rate-move-a176b0d5\n\n#ai #stocks #nvidia #stockmarket #explained #stickfigure #news",
